{"name":"Panorama","hex":"#327a88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"panorama","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An unbroken view of an entire surrounding area.","A picture or series of pictures representing a continuous scene."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/panorama"}],"entries":[{"title":"Panorama","blocks":[{"text":"A panorama is any wide-angle view or representation of a physical space, whether in painting, drawing, photography, film, seismic images, or 3D modeling. The word was coined in the 18th century by the English painter Robert Barker to describe his panoramic paintings of Edinburgh and London. The motion-picture term panning is derived from panorama."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/360%C2%B0_interior_panorama_of_San_Gregorio_church_in_Breglia%2C_Italy.jpg/330px-360%C2%B0_interior_panorama_of_San_Gregorio_church_in_Breglia%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panorama","wikidata":"Q41363"},{"title":"Panorama (British TV programme)","blocks":[{"text":"Panorama is a British current affairs documentary news programme broadcast on the BBC. First broadcast in 1953, it is the world's longest-running television news magazine programme."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5a/BBC_Panorama.png/330px-BBC_Panorama.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panorama_(British_TV_programme)","wikidata":"Q1247810"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Panorama_of_Florence.jpg/500px-Panorama_of_Florence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Panorama_of_Florence.jpg/1280px-Panorama_of_Florence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":